WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.920
She's the chief financial officer of one of
the biggest telecommunications equipment companies

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:06.290
in the world.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:10.800
Now it's emerged that Meng Wanzhou has been
in custody in Canada for days.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:16.880
US authorities appear to be seeking her extradition
on charges of helping Huawei violate the U-S

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.600
trade embargo against Iran.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.369
Further details of the allegations against
her are still unknown.

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:28.890
But her arrest comes as Huawei faces increasing
scrutiny from abroad.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:33.480
In the past, U-S lawmakers have described
the company as a threat to national security

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:38.110
- saying its technology could be used for
spying.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:43.059
Other countries, like Australia and New Zealand,
share those concerns and have banned Huawei's

00:00:43.059 --> 00:00:49.510
equipment from being used in their high-speed
5G mobile networks.

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:52.700
Huawei has repeatedly denied those claims.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:57.820
When news of Meng's arrest broke, China's
embassy in Canada released a statement saying

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:02.920
it "firmly opposes and strongly protests"
the move.

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:08.020
The arrest comes at an especially sensitive
time in US-Chinese trade relations.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:12.759
Last weekend, the countries' leaders agreed
to a 90-day truce in their months-long trade

00:01:12.759 --> 00:01:14.159
dispute.

00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:18.560
The U-S decision to target one of China's
most important tech giants is only likely

00:01:18.560 --> 00:04:02.519
to reignite tensions.

